From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:05:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] SRAM C goes to the display engine before the DE is used: out
 of reset it is the CPU's (system control 0x03000004, bit 24), and while it
 is, the DE's register window reads and writes SRAM, so mixer 0's clock and
 reset setup was lost and the panel stayed blank. TrimUI's U-Boot hands it
 over before the kernel; ours leaves the display alone, so disp_probe does it

---
 .../video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/dev_disp.c    | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/dev_disp.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/dev_disp.c
index d985ca0e1..ed208138f 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/dev_disp.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/sunxi/disp2/disp/dev_disp.c
@@ -2540,6 +2540,24 @@ static int disp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	g_disp_drv.dev = &pdev->dev;
 	pdev->dev.dma_mask = &disp_dmamask;
 
+#if defined(CONFIG_ARCH_SUN50IW10)
+	/*
+	 * SRAM C to the display engine. Out of reset it is the CPU's (system
+	 * control 0x03000004, bit 24), and while it is, the DE's registers
+	 * read and write SRAM: mixer 0 stayed in reset and the panel had no
+	 * picture. TrimUI's U-Boot hands it over before the kernel; ours
+	 * leaves the display alone, so it is done here, before the DE is used.
+	 */
+	{
+		void __iomem *sys = ioremap(0x03000004, 4);
+
+		if (sys) {
+			writel(readl(sys) & ~BIT(24), sys);
+			iounmap(sys);
+		}
+	}
+#endif
+
 	/* iomap */
 	/* de - [device(tcon-top)] - lcd0/1/2.. - dsi */
 	counter = 0;
